sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P0 as Administrator
    participant P1 as Web Application (Analytics UI)
    participant P2 as AnalyticsController
    participant P3 as Analytics Services (Report / Performance / Export)
    participant P4 as Application Database
    P0->>P1: navigateAnalyticsPage(filters)
    P1->>P2: GET /admin/analytics
    P2->>P2: authorize administrator, validate dates, filters and range
    Note over P0,P4: Authenticated, verified administrator required. Invalid filters stop the request, no report is returned.
    P2->>P4: read AnalyticsSetting::current() and layout
    P4-->>P2: return dashboard configuration
    P2->>P3: build(widgets, from, to, source, platform)
    P3->>P4: aggregate users, activity, news and broadcasts
    P4-->>P3: return aggregate rows
    P3->>P4: read selected social connections and saved Meta snapshots
    P4-->>P3: return social metrics and sync status
    P3-->>P2: return report widgets
    alt [export requested]
    P2->>P3: data(scope, filters), build CSV or XLSX
    P3->>P4: read additional export rows as required
    P4-->>P3: return export data
    P3-->>P2: return export content / workbook path
    P2-->>P1: download CSV / XLSX (private, no-store)
    P1-->>P0: save report file
    else [view dashboard]
    P2->>P3: interactionTrend(), listing(), optional post inspection
    P3->>P4: query likes, comments and post performance
    P4-->>P3: return rows and trends
    P3-->>P2: return performance data
    P2->>P4: read categories and administrator connections
    P4-->>P2: return selection options
    P2-->>P1: render admin/analytics with filters and configuration
    P1-->>P0: display charts, tables and social sync status
    end
    Note over P0,P4: Changing filters repeats GET /admin/analytics. Dashboard reads stored Meta metrics, it does not call Meta live. The generic engagement widget is still a placeholder, post performance is calculated separately.
